  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through next Sunday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: Current satellite imagery shows mostly \nclear skies with a few high clouds moving across northern Nevada. \nAn upper level high pressure system off the coast of California \nwill dominate our upper air pattern for the majority of the week, \nbringing us mostly sunny skies and afternoon highs in the upper \n50s to mid 60s. Winds are expected to remain light, except for the\nnorthern most portions of Nevada which could see up to 20 mph \ngusts Monday afternoon. Low temperatures this week are expected to\nremain in the 30s, with some areas of higher elevation seeing \nlows in the upper 20s. \n\nModels continue to show signs of an upper level trough as well as\nan atmospheric river event coming through later in the coming\nweekend. With the event being so far out, there is still plenty of\nuncertainty in the timing, placement, and strength of the event.\nModel guidance shows signals of potential rainfall and snow\nshowers associated with this trough, we will continue to monitor\nmodel trends over the next few days. \n\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: \nHigh confidence in the upper level ridge dominating the forecast\nfor the week. Low confidence on the strength and impacts of the\ntrough next weekend.",
